# Per-file escapes for sqlfluff, one entry per line, each with its reason.
# The org's sqlfluff config is delivered by the belt (lint:sql passes it with
# --config); this file is the repo-shaped half, on the same footing as
# deny.toml's skips. Nothing goes in here to silence a finding that is
# simply inconvenient.

# pgrx GENERATES this file (fix:pg-schema writes it), and lint:pg-schema owns
# it: the belt diffs freshly-generated SQL against it. sqlfluff wants LT05 and
# RF06 changes (long lines wrapped, quoted identifiers unquoted), and applying
# them means the snapshot is no longer what pgrx emits, so every later
# lint:pg-schema run diffs dirty. Removed when the belt's lint:sql skips the
# snapshot it owns.
crates/lab-pg/schema.snapshot.sql
